  "description": "VUJLIX crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C182 H170 Gd6 Mn6 N8 O56,6.5(C2 H3 N1),H2 O1. From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd6 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn3 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn4 (Mn) has 4 O neighbors; Mn5 (Mn) has 4 O neighbors; Mn6 (Mn) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 18 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.385-4.292 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 91.41-128.95°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C182H170Gd6Mn6N8O56·6.5(C2H3N)·H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 7 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 3 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies I(II).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
